WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:00.800
Hank: Good morning, John!

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:01.640
John: Good morning, Hank! It's Friday!

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.940
Hank: Question Friday; the day that we answer real questions-

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.720
John: -from real Nerdfighters. Let's get right to it!

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.920
Hank: How many times have you read The Fault in Our Stars?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.180
John: Have I? I don't know...

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.720
John: I mean, how many times have I read the finished book?

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.220
Hank: Yeah.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.360
John: The- the one that's out in hardcover?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.080
Hank: Yeah, that one.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:13.580
John: Zero.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.740
John: Why would I read it? There's lots of other books that other people wrote that I could read that I don't remember.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.000
John: How many times have you read it?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.360
Hank: Twice. I read it once before it came out, and once after it came out.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.440
John: Thanks for reading it twice.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.080
Hank: What's your favorite book series at the moment?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.940
John: My favorite book series is always gonna be Harry Potter.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.780
John: I like Divergent a lot though.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.760
Hank: Which one of you would win at an arm wrestling match?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.220
Hank: This is gonna make for a bad video.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.220
(Laughing)

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.500
John: Oh, I am gonna lose.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.560
(John shrieking)

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.360
(More laughing)

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.500
John: I mean,  I could have kept going, but I was laughing so hard.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.020
Hank: Yeah... uh huh... I won with my wit!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.340
John: Did you, Hank, ever cry to one of John's books?

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.720
Hank: Yes... I looked at it and I cried to it.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.000
John: I also have cried to one of John's books.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.620
John: If you got to give each other catchphrases what would they be?

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.180
Hank: IMAGINE COMPLEXLY!

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.660
John: Yours would actually be fart fart fart.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.900
John: How do you like your eggs?

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.080
Hank: I like them... inside of a biscuit (John: scrambled)

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.020
John: Can you please show us some family photos from when you two were younger?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.600
Hank: It's funny that you should ask because we're in the room that has the photo albums.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.720
John: I don't know if I want people to see this...

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.040
Hank: That's pretty cute. You're givin' me a little bear hug.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.540
John: Which one of you is hotter?

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.900
Hank: we'll have to have have a poll, like we're not objectively able to...

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.140
John: Right, yeah, that's perfect. That's just what I've always needed is a poll to determine whether I'm hotter than my brother.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.140
Hank: Lysh asks: Dance montage?

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.700
🎶Comic Sans is the best font in the world🎶

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.700
Hank: Do you have pizza on Thanksgiving?

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.940
John: No, we have turkey.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:32.980
Hank: We have normal Thanksgiving.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.720
John: Maybe someday we'll have turkey pizza.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.700
Hank: Favorite kind of pie?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.540
John: Pumpkin.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.920
Hank: Pumpkin also. That's a problem because there's only one pumpkin pie.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:40.880
John: Is there?

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:41.900
Hank: This Thanksgiving.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.900
John: Oh, almost like The Hunger Games

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.620
John: in that one of us is gonna be hungry and the other of us is gonna be dead.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.260
Hank: If John was a turkey and he was the last turkey on earth would you eat him for Thanksgiving?

00:01:53.020 --> 00:02:00.040
Hank: No. I mean, are there other foods available? Could I have a ham? But also if John were a turkey I probably wouldn't think very highly of you.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:07.820
John: I'm just amused by the idea that anyone, no  matter who the turkey was, would eat the last turkey on earth for Thanksgiving.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.760
John: There's only one turkey left and it is Thanksgiving.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.420
Hank: It's like when you find the last Ivory-billed Woodpecker and just be like "Well, who's gonna get to eat this?"

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.420
Hank: Could you do drawings of one another?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:17.440
John: Yeah.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:17.940
Hank: I did mine.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.800
Hank: It's sparkle pen paper.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:22.840
Hank: What do you think?

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.580
John: Ummm... yeah, I've always wanted a Hanklerfish earring.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:30.080
John: I drew Hank as well. Um, I drew him as a beaver playing the guitar.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.180
Hank: What's the worst kind of candy?

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:37.220
Hank: I think the worst kind of candy is probably a candy none of us has ever heard of because the person who created it was like "Well, that clearly is poo."

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:46.100
John: One time, uh,  I went to a contemporary art performance at which the artist, who was Chinese, handed out hard candy that tasted like crabs.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.180
John: That... was very bad candy.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.240
Hank: This person just says " Bad jokes".

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.580
John: I'd tell you a physics joke but you'd probably find it BOHRing

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.560
Hank: But, you know, jokes about Dorian Gray, they never get old.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:00.540
Hank: Is dftba.com doing anything for Black Friday?

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:08.220
John: Are we? Heck yes! There is three dollar shipping on all orders. No matter how much you order you will get it for just three dollar shipping!

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.260
Hank: Even international!

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.000
John: What?!

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.860
Hank: If you have friends and family who are looking for Christmas presents for you maybe there's something you wanna let them know about.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.480
Hank: How do you make a really good Project For Awesome video?

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:23.720
John: The key to a good Project For Awesome Video is not just like sitting in front of a camera and talking about why a charity is important to you, but actually showing it at work.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.940
Hank: And also consider the fact that you're basically pitching a charity.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.520
Hank: You have to let people know why this is important, why it's a big deal, why it's important to you personally.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.680
John: You know, the best Project for Awesome videos are also videos that the charities themselves can then use

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.180
Hank: Yeah!

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.180
John: In their own outreach to their donors.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.140
Hank: We love it when that happens, and we hope that it happens a lot this year.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.600
Hank: Have y'all always been really close?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.120
John: No, I mean we've always liked each other though

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.240
Hank: Hmm

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.080
John: Thank you for watching!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.740
Best wishes!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.740
Hank: DFTBA John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:52.840
John: Byee

